<newsitem itemid="444071" id="root" date="1997-03-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Wickes narrows 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Wickes narrows 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Loss per share (pence) 13.5	    vs 74.6</p>
<p> Pretax loss		55.7	    vs 279.3 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   583.9	   vs 834.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Wickes said like-for-like sales in Britain to the end of February 1997 were up 13 percent but down five percent on the continent. The company said it had made a &quot;satisfactory start&quot; to the year. Wickes said it did not expect to pay an interim dividend for 1997. Full name of the British home improvement chain and building products supplier is Wickes Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
